# `structure::HarmonicOptions`

Controls of the frequency-domain solve.

## Signature

```cpp
structure::HarmonicOptions
```

## What It Does

Controls for `harmonic`, which solves `(K + i omega C - omega^2 M) u = f` with a restarted GMRES iteration at each frequency.

## Fields

| Field | Meaning | Default |
|---|---|---|
| `mass_damping` | The coefficient `a` of `a M`; the damping ratio of mode `n` is `a / (2 omega_n)`. | `0` |
| `stiffness_damping` | The coefficient `b` of `b K`; the damping ratio of mode `n` is `b omega_n / 2`. | `0` |
| `solve` | GMRES controls: `max_iterations` (128), `restart` (24), `relative_tolerance` (1e-8), `absolute_tolerance` (1e-10), `rank_tolerance` (1e-12). A larger frame may need a longer restart and a larger budget. |  |
| `fail_on_nonconvergence` | When true a frequency whose solve does not converge throws; when false `converged` is false at that frequency. A frequency at a natural frequency of an undamped frame is singular by physics and does not converge. | `true` |

## Returns

A value; validated by `harmonic`.

## Errors

Negative damping coefficients or invalid GMRES controls are rejected.

## Interpretation and Use

Damping is what keeps the response finite at a natural frequency: with none the amplitude grows without bound as the frequency approaches one, and exactly at it the dynamic stiffness is singular and the solve reports nonconvergence.

